# Database (Supabase/Postgres)

- Every table with tenant-scoped data has `gym_org_id`. Every query MUST
  filter on it — either via RLS policy or an explicit WHERE clause. Never
  rely on "we'll filter it in the frontend."
- Prefer Postgres Row Level Security policies for read paths queried
  directly from the client via Supabase JS. Write paths that mutate
  billing, invites, or grants go through the Express API, not direct
  client writes — flag it if you see a direct client-side `.insert()` /
  `.update()` on a sensitive table (plans, invoices, grants, invites).
- Migrations are additive and reversible. Never write a migration that
  drops a column without an explicit ask.
- Price/billing snapshots are immutable once written — never write an
  UPDATE against a stored invoice/snapshot row; corrections are new rows.
- Use parameterized queries / the Supabase query builder — never
  string-concatenate SQL.
